+
+## Safe local extension smoke check
+
+`ops/local-extension-smoke.mjs` opens a fresh headed Chromium profile and serves
+an invented Granot form at `http://localhost:3411`. It sends the real extension
+`PING` and read-only `PARSE_TARIFF_ADJUSTMENT` messages and asserts the response.
+It does not sign in, read credentials, submit a form, or call Vantage APIs.
+Localhost is already included in the extension's existing URL permissions.
+
+Run `pnpm build` first. With Playwright available to Node:
+
+```powershell
+node ops/local-extension-smoke.mjs
+```
+
+If Playwright is supplied by the Codex bundled runtime, set
+`PLAYWRIGHT_MODULE` to its absolute `playwright/index.mjs` path. Set
+`GRANOT_CHROMIUM_PATH` to a Playwright Chromium `chrome.exe` when its installed
+version differs from Playwright's default. Branded Chrome can ignore extension
+sideload flags; use Playwright Chromium for this harness.
+
+Pass `--keep-open` to keep the isolated browser and fixture running after the
+assertions. Its CDP endpoint is `http://127.0.0.1:9223`; Ctrl+C closes both.
+Ports 3411 and 9223 must be free. The temporary profile is printed for cleanup
+and stays outside the repository. The harness never loads the saved customer
+HTML. WXT's separate hot-reload server uses port 3400.
+
+For a repeatable setup with the pinned Playwright dependency (Node 22+):
+
+```powershell
+pnpm install
+pnpm exec playwright install chromium
+pnpm build
+pnpm dev:browser
+```
+
+From another terminal, `pnpm browser:readiness` connects to that browser and
+checks only the synthetic form. `pnpm test:browser` launches and closes its own
+isolated browser instead; stop `dev:browser` first so the ports are free.
+
+`pnpm browser:readiness --inspect-current-job` reads exactly one already-open
+Granot Charges / Forms View tab. Open a supported job manually first. It sends
+only PING and the read-only parser message, checks CF/ZIP availability plus
+Distance and two state/ZIP pairs in the DOM, and prints booleans only. It does
+not navigate, change fields, calculate pricing or print customer values.
+
+`pnpm browser:readiness --live` explicitly opens a separate Granot login tab,
+completes the two login stages and checks extension PING. It stops at Main Menu;
+report/job navigation remains manual. This mode reads the local workspace
+`../agent_granot_credentials/.env` (override with `GRANOT_CREDENTIALS_FILE`).
+Supported aliases are `GRANOT_NETWORK_USERNAME` / `MAIN_LOGIN_USERNAME`,
+`GRANOT_NETWORK_PASSWORD` / `MAIN_LOGIN_PASSWORD`, `GRANOT_USERNAME` /
+`SPECIFIC_USERNAME`, and `GRANOT_PASSWORD` / `SPECIFIC_PASSWORD`. Process
+environment values take precedence. Credentials stay in memory and the login
+form; logs omit credentials, raw errors, page URLs, titles and customer values.
+Both connected modes preserve existing tabs and disconnect without closing
+the developer's browser. Live login requires the currently documented Granot
+form shape. Synthetic, live-login and current-job modes were verified on
+October 25, 2026; the current-job mode reads one sample and is not a claim of
+coverage across every Granot form variant.
 
